+// v8xx PTF (b2349, b2381; RSTL fold option 1, adapted once after ptf30's PCQ FAIL): after the turn's last act, the dense travel rows
+// (and the stages before them) are built in leftover fuel, each only when its cost estimate + PTF_TAB[4] fits, so the engine never cuts
+// them (no planned cut, no resume). The k-list closure stays in the background as live: its tvm_gen bumps void the TVM memo, and run
+// after the actions they made the next turns' compute_travel recompute (ptf30: dense-call fuel 4.8k v 4.0k). No fill on a turn that
+// ended under PTF_TAB[3] fuel or within AF_HEAVY_KEEP rounds of a bailed or suspended turn. No action, comms, travel stamp or meter.
+int ptf_round = -1;
+bool ptf_fill()
+{
+	if (fuel() < PTF_TAB[3] || W.round - af_heavy_round <= AF_HEAVY_KEEP)
+		return false; // the neutral rule (first: the cheapest test)
